From 3b480064703874811276c8a4ccfa6e48dfaa17fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hakkabon <dev@example.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 06:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] NumericCoreAMPL: implement lexer, parser, and presolve
 for the grammar in docs/design/ampl-grammar.md

Model gains addParameter/addConstraint/setObjective (previously only
addVariable existed), plus LinearExpression/RelationalOperator/
Objective/Constraint types.

- AMPLLexer.swift: hand-rolled tokenizer (keyword/identifier/number/
  symbol), plus '#' line comments (not in the EBNF, needed for any
  real model file).
- AMPLParser.swift: hand-rolled recursive descent, calling Model's
  builder methods directly (no intermediate AST - the grammar's small
  enough that one isn't earning its complexity yet). One documented
  extension beyond the literal EBNF: a linear_expr may start with a
  leading +/- before its first term. Identifier resolution in a term
  checks variables first, then params (a param reference folds into
  the expression's constant at parse time) - this is what actually
  makes param_decl useful, since the EBNF's term production doesn't
  otherwise distinguish the two.
- Presolve.swift: Model.compile() -> CompiledProblem. A maximize
  objective is negated to minimize form; CompiledProblem.objectiveSign
  records +1/-1 so a caller can flip a solver's result back to the
  model's original sense. Row bounds derived by moving each
  constraint's rhs to the lhs and reading the resulting relop.

Not built on the hakkabon/Grammar/Lexer/Parser packages the original
design sketch called for - their exact public APIs weren't available
to write against here, so a small self-contained implementation was
chosen over guessing at an external API (documented in Model.swift's
module docs as a real, isolated migration option once those APIs are
in hand).

Tests: AMPLLexerTests (tokenization, two-char-symbol-before-prefix,
comments, unrecognized-character throws), AMPLParserTests (the exact
example model from ampl-grammar.md, param folding, leading-negative
extension, unknown-identifier throws), PresolveTests (the same example
model compiled to the documented CompiledProblem shape, minimize vs
maximize sign handling, equality constraints, variables-on-both-sides,
empty-constraint-set, no-objective throws).

Not yet done: wiring CompiledProblem through NCBindings to
nc-optimize::Solver (still StubSolver) - see updated
docs/design/ampl-grammar.md's Next steps.

Updates docs/design/ampl-grammar.md (marked implemented, corrected the
worked example's objective sign to match the real negate-for-maximize
behavior) and README.md (also reflects the LU and zero-copy-buffer
work from the two preceding commits, since all three landed in the
same session).
